{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f61_2_dropped_channel_margin_f61_2", "label": "Fault F61.2 \u2014 dmargin and ORDER_MATCH compare unlike channel sets", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F61.2-DROPPED-CHANNEL-MARGIN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f61_2_dropped_channel_margin_dropped_channel_artifact", "label": "The dropped-channel margin artifact", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F61.2-DROPPED-CHANNEL-MARGIN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "nlchain filters to converged channels before sorting, so a seed that kills the runner-up widens the margin without moving a single eigenvalue. At Z=19 the printed 35 mHa 'seed effect' is entirely the missing 4p; on the A\u2229B intersection the same quantity agrees to 0.02 mHa. Three ORDER_MATCH=false values are not order changes."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f61_2_dropped_channel_margin_intersection_baseline", "label": "Score on the intersection, against the harness's own baseline row", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F61.2-DROPPED-CHANNEL-MARGIN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two independent defects: the baseline was the sealed (pre-guard) row that F61.1's own remedy forbids, and margin is computed over surviving channels only. F61.1 recorded that remedy as Done and the code was never changed \u2014 a ruling that reaches no artefact is R 1670's finding: a practice with no file behind it."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f61_2_dropped_channel_margin_convergence_floor", "label": "The convergence floor \u2014 a worse seed costs channels, not values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F61.2-DROPPED-CHANNEL-MARGIN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "capt